	<description><![CDATA[County-domain (SINGLE) inventory for Washtenaw with TIME AGGREGATION by
year (<aggregateBy key="Year"/>, <outputtimestep value="Year"/>; January, April,
July and October 2020, both day types, all hours -- scale-county-timeagg-processes-year's
collapse), the Year twin of scale-county-evap-species: for the gasoline passenger car (21) and the diesel combination long-haul truck
(62), road types 1 and 4: EVERY pollutant MOVES 5 associates with evaporative
permeation, fuel vapor venting and fuel leaks (11, 12, 13) and refueling
displacement and spillage (18, 19) in pollutantProcessAssoc -- THC, the
hydrocarbon chain (NMHC, NMOG, TOG, VOC; methane and NonHAPTOG at 18 and 19
only, where they are pairs), the air toxics (benzene and ethanol from
ATRatioNonGas, 2,2,4-trimethylpentane, ethyl benzene, hexane, toluene and
xylene from minorHAPRatio, naphthalene gas) and the NonHAPTOG mechanism
(3000). No exhaust, wear or crankcase process. County database
county-inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg/setup-timeagg.sql.]]></description>
